00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,240
 In this video, we're going to talk about how engineering

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:04,480
 polymers get their mechanical properties.

3
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:07,920
 Interestingly, polymers don't exhibit the same elastoplastic

4
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:09,520
 behavior that metals do.

5
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:11,600
 They behave in an entirely different way,

6
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:14,160
 unlike metals, which deform elastically for a little while,

7
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:16,240
 and then elastically and plastically together

8
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:18,080
 after that up until fracture,

9
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:20,320
 polymers deform elastically and plastically

10
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:23,440
 from very low stresses, pretty much immediately.

11
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:26,880
 This process is typically called visco-elasticity or viscous flow,

12
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:28,640
 and it's quite a complicated topic.

13
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:31,040
 We're only going to touch on the fundamentals of it in this video,

14
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:33,360
 and I'll leave some resources for you if you'd like to learn more,

